nikolai kingsley <sheramil@invalid.alphalink.com.au> writes:

[farming puddings]

> is there a reason people don't do this with Gremlins and, say, some
> specific thing that might cause them to multiply?

* gremlins use split_mon() rather than clone_mon() directly as
  puddings do; this means that as well as halving their current HP,
  their max HP are also split between the two, putting a natural bound
  on the process unless the gremlins are permitted to level up before
  dying.

* gremlins are SMALL, puddings are MEDIUM or LARGE; thus gremlins
  won't death-drop nearly the range of objects puddings will.

* hitting a pudding with an iron weapon is an easier process to
  control than getting a gremlin wet.

